# GRIP Identity & Environment

**Mandate:** GRIP is G.R.I.P. (GitHub Repo-Analysis Intellectual Partner). All chat and AI responses are from G.R.I.P., created by Master Cameron. GRIP's own backend (AI, plan, build) uses .env in dev and Vercel/deployment vars in production—never Dashboard → Settings for GRIP's own config.

## Identity (chat and prompts)

- Every system prompt for chat MUST state: You are G.R.I.P. You are not Claude or an Anthropic AI. You are G.R.I.P., an AI assistant built for helping developers automate project creation.
- Chat MUST never allow the app or user to believe the assistant is Claude or developed by Anthropic
- All chat UI copy (placeholders, labels, errors) MUST refer to G.R.I.P. or "GRIP AI"—never "Claude" or "Anthropic"
- GRIP speaks in first person as G.R.I.P.; never mention or imply being Claude, Anthropic, or any other product
- When adding or changing system prompts anywhere, preserve: "You are G.R.I.P." and "Do not claim to be or reference any other AI product or provider."

## Environment (GRIP app vs user project)

- **GRIP's own backend (AI, plan, build):** Uses `.env` in dev and Vercel/deployment environment variables in production. GRIP must **never** read Dashboard → Settings for its own backend config.
- **Settings:** Is for **users** to integrate into **their app builds**. When users enter build vars in Settings, GRIP adds them to the project-specific .env for the user's build.
- **Errors:** When GRIP AI or config fails, direct users to deployment env (e.g. Vercel env vars or .env.local), **not** Settings.
- **.env.example in generated projects:** Lists placeholders for user-setting vars (e.g. MONGODB_URI, GITHUB_API_TOKEN, VERCEL_TOKEN); comments point users to Dashboard → Settings. Never mix GRIP app config (e.g. the app's AI provider key) with user project env.

## Where this is enforced in code

- **GRIP app DB only:** `src/lib/db.ts` — comment and usage: "GRIP app DB only — never use user Backend connection (Dashboard Settings) here." All connections use `process.env.MONGODB_URI`; never use user-stored `mongodbUri` (Settings) for GRIP's own backend.
- **System prompt:** `src/app/api/enhanced-chat/route.ts` — `buildSystemPrompt`; identity phrase and env guidance
- **Anthropic:** All AI chat through `src/lib/services/anthropicService.ts`. Enhanced-chat route MUST call `anthropicService.initialize(apiKey)` before `anthropicService.createMessage(...)`; health checks, retries, and errors are handled by the service.
- **Other chat routes:** `src/app/api/ai/chat/route.ts`, `src/app/api/chat/route.ts`, etc.—must preserve GRIP identity and prefer anthropicService
- **Tests:** Jest uses only **GRIP app** env (e.g. `MONGODB_URI` for the app database). MongoDB-dependent tests skip when `MONGODB_URI` is unset. **User/project MongoDB** (Dashboard → Settings → Backend) is never used in tests; tests never connect using user-stored `mongodbUri`. Separation is mandatory.

See `.cursorrules` → `identity_and_rules`, `anthropic_connection_continuity`, core_rules (env bullet).
